    audience: "French-speaking skilled workers considering permanent residence",
    focus: "the NCLC language threshold, eligible work experience and profile evidence",
    eligibility: "French category eligibility begins with a valid French test in all four abilities and eligibility for at least one Express Entry program. The category is a selection priority, not a replacement for the federal program rules.",
    evidence: "Keep the language certificate, test date, passport identity details and the work evidence supporting the NOC and TEER code together. Informal fluency is not a substitute for an accepted language result.",
